  "jlc_stock_review": [
   {
    "index": 0,
    "holds": false,
    "line": 299,
    "reason": "The digikey-route branch (second_source text matching 'second vendor', the majority of rows) never reads row.alt at all -- only rows whose second_source matches the 'alternate' pattern (jlc_by_part(row.alt) at line 324) get their alternate re-queried at JLCPCB. For a normal row (e.g. ABM8-272-T3, MCP2518FDT-E/SL) the Alternate column's part is never queried anywhere, so the script does not re-query JLCPCB 'for each row's alternate' in general, only for the few rows on the alternate route."
   },
   {
    "index": 1,
    "holds": true,
    "line": 137,
    "reason": "jlc_by_lcsc filters the JLCPCB keyword-search results for componentCode.upper() == lcsc.upper(), i.e. the result whose LCSC number equals the row's."
   },
   {
    "index": 2,
    "holds": true,
    "line": 237,
    "reason": "gate(boards, placements) returns max(5*boards*placements, 50), implementing sourcing rule 4 exactly as the docstring (line 7) states."
   },
   {
    "index": 3,
    "holds": true,
    "line": 391,
    "reason": "_check_r4 appends a problem when jlc_by_lcsc returns 'no_match' (line 282), and main() returns 1 when --check is set and problems is non-empty (line 391), so an LCSC with no exact JLCPCB match exits 1."
   },
   {
    "index": 4,
    "holds": true,
    "line": 343,
    "reason": "In the alternate branch, when the alternate's own stock/presale check fails (not ok) and the row's own rule-4 check failed too (not r4_ok), a problem is appended, causing exit 1 only when both fail."
   },
   {
    "index": 5,
    "holds": true,
    "line": 348,
    "reason": "After the fix applied in this review, the branch '(not r4_ok) and ok' (row fails rule 4, its alternate passes) prints '[warn] ... covered by alternate ...' and adds no problem; before the fix this case was silently printed as [ok] and the unrelated case (alternate fails, row passes) was mislabeled 'warn' instead."
   },
   {
    "index": 6,
    "holds": true,
    "line": 304,
    "reason": "The digikey-route branch calls dk_stock(row.part, dk_head) (line 304), and the off-board branch calls it for the part (line 314) and, when an alternate exists, for the alternate too (line 319); dk_head comes from dk_credentials()/dk_headers(), i.e. DIGIKEY_CLIENT_ID and DIGIKEY_CLIENT_SECRET (or DIGIKEY_ENV_FILE)."
   },
   {
    "index": 7,
    "holds": false,
    "line": 316,
    "reason": "The off-board part's own check is required=True unconditionally (line 316), so it forces exit 1 whenever the part alone is under gate even if its alternate has ample stock -- the alternate cannot rescue it, unlike the on-board 'alternate, rule 5' branch (sentence 4) where both must fail. Conversely when the part passes and only the alternate is under gate, required=not primary_ok is False (line 321), so that case never triggers exit 1 by itself (only warn). Neither half matches a plain 'the part or its alternate is under the gate' reading, and the 'since the alternate is its only second source' framing implies the alternate should be able to cover a primary shortfall, which the code does not let it do."
   },
   {
    "index": 8,
    "holds": true,
    "line": 270,
    "reason": "When dk_head is None, 'Digi-Key not checked: no credentials' is appended to problems (line 270, forcing exit 1 under --check), and each digikey-route or off-board row prints its own '[??] ... not checked, no Digi-Key credentials' line (lines 301-302, 311-312)."
   },
   {
    "index": 9,
    "holds": true,
    "line": 256,
    "reason": "Rows with row.held truthy are collected into held_rows and printed under their own 'Personal library (rule 6, export of {HELD_DATE})' header (lines 256-258), separate from the per-row rule-4/rule-5 loop, with HELD_DATE ('2026-09-25') being the date the held quantity was stated."
   },
   {
    "index": 10,
    "holds": true,
    "line": 19,
    "reason": "The docstring states this directly, and it is corroborated by CONTRIBUTING.md's 'What CI checks' list and ci.yml, neither of which invokes tools/jlc_stock.py; only tools/research/session.py is run in CI for the research scripts."
   }
  ]
 }
